rican (New), Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"-Tskf8WK17rb3ZfeFuRSWA","review_id":"iolJUgBGFv-U0KMvVT7EjA","date":"2015-11-27T17:42:14","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9495254755020142,"text_excerpt":"OK Yelp reader - repeat after me - \"I am going to come to the Palace Cafe and eat the crab cheesecake!\" Say it again.... and again... then go do it. Yes it's that good, that no trip to New Orleans is complete without it. 5+++++ stars and is truly one of the greatest things I've eaten in my life. Those that know my yelp reviews, know that I don't make such statements lightly. It's only $9.50 and listed as an appetizer. It's on their breakfast, brunch, lunch, and dinner menu. It's their signature dish, so you have no excuse not get it. You don't have a large dining budget you say? No problem, don't have a whole meal at the Palace Cafe, just order a slice of the crab cheesecake and sit at an..."},{"business_id":"-Tskf8WK17rb3ZfeFuRSWA","review_id":"8ItTuVvzlmGU2wQwYQXtiA","date":"2014-01-09T23:05:22","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9419365525245667,"text_excerpt":"I love this place for really good New Orleans/ Creole style cooking. I usually stop in for dessert, usually Bananas Foster (pretty presentation) or White Chocolate Bread Pudding (It's not the best bread pudding in town, but the only place I know of that serves it made this way). The ambiance and decor is beautiful, and the food presentation is great. The last time I ate there was a Sunday brunch and the service was slow. I met my group late and the server didn't notice me for about ten minutes, but once she did, she made it her best to take my food and drink orders and get everything out in a timely manner so that I could \"catch up\" with the rest of the table."},{"business_id":"-Tskf8WK17rb3ZfeFuRSWA","review_id":"v1839mnhu4ZSGVQ6Dp9nqA","date":"2017-05-26T19:22:23","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9388142228126526,"text_excerpt":"No joke: we would have eaten all 3 meals a day at Palace Cafe during our Nola trip. We had brunch here on our 1st day and sat in the upstairs Black Duck Bar/Lounge which had a full service menu. I had the crab cheesecake (savory and outstanding), the white bean garlic soup (meh). My hubby had the Croque Madame (was like a toasted ham and cheese with fried egg on top, hollandaise sauce).. he liked it a lot (didn't love) but was worth trying. We thought the bar service that day was friendly but not totally attentive (we sat at the bar). The next day we opted to sit in the main dining room. Recommend sitting in the upstairs dining since it's quieter but the wait was too long. Our dinner expe..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"-Tskf8WK17rb3ZfeFuRSWA","photo_id":"pCv-_C5fH8B_NILUs5D_Gw","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/pCv-_C5fH8B_NILUs5D_Gw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.873956561088562},{"business_id":"-Tskf8WK17rb3ZfeFuRSWA","photo_id":"RtGPvIo_7wk3YYtWS5rUJg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/RtGPvIo_7wk3YYtWS5rUJg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8436517119407654},{"business_id":"-Tskf8WK17rb3ZfeFuRS